-- title:
--   Hecke set at the ramified prime is a single coset
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $p$ be a prime such that `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b p` holds, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $p\in v$. Let $X$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and $M\in\mathbb{N}$ with `IsEichlerOrder X M`, i.e. $X=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ with the relative index of $X$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $M$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime with $p\in v$, and let $\varpi$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose local component at every height-one prime $w$ with $p\notin w$ equals $1$, and which lies in `primeHeckeSet X p`: that is, $\varpi$ lies in the finite adelic box $\widehat{X}$ (the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in X$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele), $p\varpi^{-1}\in\widehat X$, while $\varpi^{-1}\notin\widehat X$ and $p^{-1}\varpi\notin\widehat X$. Write $U=$ [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer X`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26) for the stabiliser of $\widehat X$ in the idele units, and let the class set be the double coset quotient of the idele units by the image of the diagonal $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ on the left and $U$ on the right. Then three assertions hold: (i) `primeHeckeSet X p` is exactly the right coset $\{\varpi u : u\in U\}$; (ii) for all classes $x,y$, the Hecke kernel `heckeKernel U (primeHeckeSet X p) x y`, the number of cosets $cU$ arising as $hU$ for some $h$ in the Hecke set with $x_{\mathrm{out}}h$ lying in the class $y$, equals $1$ when `classSetShift _ ϖ x = y`, i.e. when $y$ is the class of $x_{\mathrm{out}}\varpi$, and $0$ otherwise; and (iii) for any finiteness of the class set and any $f:\mathrm{ClassSet}\to\mathbb{Z}$, the matrix `classSetHeckeMatrix U (primeHeckeSet X p)`, with $(i,j)$ entry the kernel at $(j,i)$, sends $f$ to $f\circ$ `classSetShift _ ϖ`.
--
--   This is the classical statement that at a prime dividing the discriminant of a definite quaternion algebra the Hecke operator $T_p$ on an Eichler order has degree one and coincides with the Atkin–Lehner shift by a local uniformiser, so that the corresponding Brandt matrix is the permutation matrix of that shift. It is used in the comparison of the class-set Hecke module with the Čerednik–Drinfeld side, where the Hecke clause at $\ell=p$ must be read off as a permutation of vertices and edges.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsEichlerOrder_primeHeckeSet_eq_and_heckeKernel_eq_of_ramified.lean

